Description: Finger scrolling as a touchpad's smooth scrolling
 Scrolling the compositor marks with axis_source finger comes from a new
 "xwayland-touchpad" slave device of X input type TOUCHPAD, with the motion of
 the same frames, as XI2.1 smooth scroll valuators in X pixels. One increment is
 the device's "Xwayland Scroll Pixel Distance" (CARD32, 120 until the compositor
 sets it). Clients that read the device type (Chromium) scroll by the pixels sent
 rather than animating wheel steps. Scroll events that would follow another
 device's, and each finger sequence, start with an event that moves the scroll
 valuators by nothing, so clients that reset their baseline when the core pointer
 switches devices or enters a window lose no delta. Wheel and value120 scrolling
 stays on the pointer device.
Forwarded: not-needed
